---
type: regression-verification
title: Celly incomplete ownership history startup crash
description: Keep the native CLI alive while refusing delivery without verifiable ownership history.
timestamp: 2026-10-20
tags: [celly, crash, ownership, corrupt-history]
---

# Observed

Celly sandbox G:/ciel-bridge-service router instance 9385-52ea0f8a2296 at
2026-10-20T18:07:05 logged pending_poll -> begin_attempt -> _items line 243;
routed exit diagnostic at 18:07:07 identifies e7d81c7. The deployed line raises
wake ownership history contains an incomplete record. Existing prior logs
already recorded strict reconciliation failure for incomplete history. That
condition was not covered by the previous startup acceptance.

Actual status history could not be opened: WinError 5 for the sandbox workspace
status directory/file. Windows sudo is disabled. No ACL/config repair or user
history mutation was attempted; damaged line contents and origin remain unknown.

# Fix boundary

Strict parsing now raises typed WakeHistoryUnavailable with a line number,
without logging raw rows. The pending poll catches this pre-send condition,
keeps cursor/marker/inflight unchanged, rate-limits a delivery_held diagnostic,
and leaves the CLI running. It does not treat unknown history as an empty queue
or completion proof. A post-submit instance of the same exception cannot become
a safe retry. Claim cleanup retains its existing fail-closed rules.

# Verification

76 focused tests passed. New epoch-bound real-poll tests cover incomplete tail,
malformed middle row and blank row: no send, no ownership/cursor write, no crash,
bounded polling/logging. Restoring only the owned test fixture resumes delivery.
Post-send history errors remain non-retryable. 296 adjacent tests ran with zero
failures/errors and 80 skips. Ruff and architecture checks passed. Native
corrupt-history fixture acceptance is recorded after completion.

# Limits

This fixes session termination, not corrupted user data. While the real durable
history is unverifiable, external input remains held rather than replayed.
No live Celly/Walkie restart or sandbox deployment is performed automatically.


# Native harness iterations

First owned run proved the CLI remained alive and held delivery during corrupt
history. The script then timed out because its request marker was not in the
fixture's recognized marker allowlist, even though rendered STUB-REPLY-3 and
socket/confirmation logs showed delivery after owned-fixture restoration.
Second iteration exited on a harness psutil.NoSuchProcess race during process
sampling before the corruption test. Neither is counted as full acceptance.
The dedicated third iteration catches vanished sampling children and verifies
only corrupt-history startup, no-send, and owned-fixture recovery. No live
workspace data is repaired by the harness.

Native third iteration passed: CLI alive during corruption, no transport send
without ownership history, held input replied after owned-fixture restoration,
and router listener absent after teardown. See evidence/native-source.json.
